#include-once

#cs ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

    Routes.au3

    The waypoints each zone is walked through, one function per zone.

    A route is deliberately dumb: it is only "where to walk next". The
    pathfinder finds the way between two waypoints and fights everything inside
    its aggro range on the way, so a route does not need to describe how to get
    anywhere or what to kill - a loop around the zone that passes every spawn is
    enough. If the zone is not clear when the route ends the controller simply
    runs it again.

    ADDING A ZONE
        1. Add Func Route_<Name>() below, returning an [n][2] array of x/y.
        2. Point the map's Route column in Maps.au3 at "<Name>".

    The coordinates come from mrdomrocks' Guild Wars Vanquish Bot (MIT), which
    is the reference implementation these routes were verified against:
    https://github.com/mrdomrocks/Guild-Wars-Vanquish-Bot

#ce ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

;~ Description: The waypoints registered under a route name, or an error when
;~              nothing is registered under it.
Func Routes_Get($sRouteName)
	If $sRouteName = "" Then Return SetError(1, 0, 0)

	Local $aRoute = Call("Route_" & $sRouteName)
	If @error = 0xDEAD And @extended = 0xBEEF Then Return SetError(1, 0, 0)
	If Not IsArray($aRoute) Then Return SetError(2, 0, 0)

	Return $aRoute
EndFunc   ;==>Routes_Get

